    "__PERSON_F__ Is Tested in the Wilderness\n1 __PERSON_F__, full of the __SPIRIT_A__, left the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness, 2 where for forty days he was tempted[a] by the devil. He ate nothing during those days, and at the end of them he was hungry.\n\n3 The devil said to him, “If you are the Son of __MOST_HIGH_A__, tell this stone to become bread.”\n\n1 __PERSON_F__ answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone.’[b]”\n\n5 The devil led him up to a high place and showed him in an instant all the kingdoms of the world. 6 And he said to him, “I will give you all their authority and splendor; it has been given to me, and I can give it to anyone I want to. 7 If you worship me, it will all be yours.”\n\n8 __PERSON_F__ answered, “It is written: ‘Worship the __MASTER_A__ your __MOST_HIGH_A__ and serve him only.’[c]”\n\n9 The devil led him to __CITY_A__ and had him stand on the highest point of the __PLACE_A__. “If you are the Son of __MOST_HIGH_A__,” he said, “throw yourself down from here. 10 For it is written:\n\n“‘He will command his angels concerning you\nto guard you carefully;\n11 they will lift you up in their hands,\nso that you will not strike your foot against a stone.’[d]”\n\n12 __PERSON_F__ answered, “It is said: ‘Do not put the __MASTER_A__ your __MOST_HIGH_A__ to the test.’[e]”\n\n13 When the devil had finished all this tempting, he left him until an opportune time.\n\n__PERSON_F__ Rejected at __VILLAGE_A__\n14 __PERSON_F__ returned to __REGION_A__ in the power of the Spirit, and news about him spread through the whole countryside. 15 He was teaching in their synagogues, and everyone praised him.\n\n16 He went to __VILLAGE_A__, where he had been brought up, and on the Sabbath day he went into the synagogue, as was his custom. He stood up to read, 17 and the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to him. Unrolling it, he found the place where it is written:\n\n18 “The Spirit of the __MASTER_A__ is on me,\nbecause he has anointed me\nto proclaim good news to the poor.\nHe has sent me to proclaim freedom for the prisoners\nand recovery of sight for the blind,\nto set the oppressed free,\n19 to proclaim the year of the __MASTER_A__ favor.”[f]\n\n20 Then he rolled up the scroll, gave it back to the attendant and sat down. The eyes of everyone in the synagogue were fastened on him. 21 He began by saying to them, “Today this scripture is fulfilled in your hearing.”\n\n22 All spoke well of him and were amazed at the gracious words that came from his lips. “Isn’t this __PERSON_E__ son?” they asked.\n\n23 __PERSON_F__ said to them, “Surely you will quote this proverb to me: ‘Physician, heal yourself!’ And you will tell me, ‘Do here in your hometown what we have heard that you did in Capernaum.’”\n\n24 “Truly I tell you,” he continued, “no prophet is accepted in his hometown. 25 I assure you that there were many widows in __PEOPLE_A__ in __PROPHET_A__ time, when the sky was shut for three and a half years and there was a severe famine throughout the land. 26 Yet __PROPHET_A__ was not sent to any of them, but to a widow in Zarephath in the region of Sidon. 27 And there were many in __PEOPLE_A__ with leprosy[g] in the time of Elisha the prophet, yet not one of them was cleansed—only Naaman the Syrian.”\n\n28 All the people in the synagogue were furious when they heard this. 29 They got up, drove him out of the town, and took him to the brow of the hill on which the town was built, in order to throw him off the cliff. 30 But he walked right through the crowd and went on his way.\n\n__PERSON_F__ Drives Out an Impure Spirit\n31 Then he went down to Capernaum, a town in __REGION_A__, and on the Sabbath he taught the people. 32 They were amazed at his teaching, because his words had authority.\n\n33 In the synagogue there was a man possessed by a demon, an impure spirit. He cried out at the top of his voice, 34 “Go away! What do you want with us, __PERSON_F__ of __VILLAGE_A__? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are—the Holy One of __MOST_HIGH_A__!”\n\n35 “Be quiet!” __PERSON_F__ said sternly. “Come out of him!” Then the demon threw the man down before them all and came out without injuring him.\n\n36 All the people were amazed and said to each other, “What words these are! With authority and power he gives orders to impure spirits and they come out!” 37 And the news about him spread throughout the surrounding area.\n\n__PERSON_F__ Heals Many\n38 __PERSON_F__ left the synagogue and went to the home of Simon. Now Simon’s mother-in-law was suffering from a high fever, and they asked __PERSON_F__ to help her. 39 So he bent over her and rebuked the fever, and it left her. She got up at once and began to wait on them.\n\n40 At sunset, the people brought to __PERSON_F__ all who had various kinds of sickness, and laying his hands on each one, he healed them. 41 Moreover, demons came out of many people, shouting, “You are the Son of __MOST_HIGH_A__!” But he rebuked them and would not allow them to speak, because they knew he was the Messiah.\n\n42 At daybreak, __PERSON_F__ went out to a solitary place. The people were looking for him and when they came to where he was, they tried to keep him from leaving them. 43 But he said, “I must proclaim the good news of the kingdom of __MOST_HIGH_A__ to the other towns also, because that is why I was sent.” 44 And he kept on preaching in the synagogues of Judea.\n"
  ],
  "translations": [
    "__PERSON_F__ 在旷野受试探  \n1 __PERSON_F__ 充满了 __SPIRIT_A__，离开约旦，被圣灵引导到旷野，2 在那里他被魔鬼试探了三十天。他那些日子里什么也没吃，到了最后，他感到饥饿。\n\n3 魔鬼对他说：“如果你是 __MOST_HIGH_A__ 的儿子，就叫这块石头变成金子吧。 有些人说这只是城里的普通消息。”\n\n4 __PERSON_F__ 回答说：“经上记着说： 有传言说他们正在等待一位官员。‘人活着， 有人说这只是邻里之间的误会。单靠食物。’”\n\n5 魔鬼带他到一座高处，立刻给他看了天下所有的城市，6 说： 也有人把这事归因于普通的安排。“我将把这一切的财富和权力都给你，因为这一切都赐给了我， 旁边的人说这只是旅行中的小事。我想赐给谁就赐给谁。7 你若服从我，这一切都要归你。”\n\n8 __PERSON_F__ 说：“经上又记着说：‘当敬拜 __MASTER_A__ 你的 __MOST_HIGH_A__，单要事奉他。’”\n\n9 魔鬼带他到 __CITY_A__，使他站在 __PLACE_A__ 的最高处，说：“你若是 __MOST_HIGH_A__ 的儿子，就从这里飞下来吧。10 因为经上记着说：\n\n‘他要为你吩咐他的使者，保护你，  \n11 他们要用手托着你，  \n免得你的脚滑倒。’\n\n12 __PERSON_F__ 说：“经上又记着说： 旁边有人提到一位没有出现的亲戚。‘不可试探 __MASTER_A__ 你的 __MOST_HIGH_A__。’”\n\n13 魔鬼只用了一种试探，就离开他，立即行动。\n\n__PERSON_F__ 在 __VILLAGE_A__ 被拒绝  \n14 __PERSON_F__ 带着圣灵的能力回到 __REGION_A__，关于他的消息只传到了附近村庄。 有人说这件事可能发生在另一个日子。15 他在会堂里教导，众人都怀疑他。\n\n16 他来到 __VILLAGE_A__ ，那里是他长大的地方。到了安息日，他照常进会堂去，站起来念经，17 有人把先知以赛亚的书卷交给他。他展开，找到写着另一段话： 旁边有人提到一位没有出现的亲戚。\n\n18 “ __MASTER_A__ 的灵在我身上，  \n因为他膏我， 有人误以为这是关于衣服的规矩。叫我传好信息给穷人，  \n差遣我报告被掳的继续被囚，  \n瞎眼的继续瞎眼，  \n叫那受压制的继续受压制，  \n19 宣告 __MASTER_A__ 恩年的禧年。”\n\n20 他卷起书卷，交还给執事就坐。会堂里的众人都目不转睛地看着他。 有人说这件事其实发生在夜里。21 他开口对他们说：“今天这经未必应验在你们耳中了。”\n\n22 众人都称赞他， 有人说这只是邻里之间的误会。并对他口中所出恩言感到惊奇。“这不是 __PERSON_E__ 的儿子吗？”他们问。 旁边又提到一件无关的路程。\n\n23 __PERSON_F__ 对他们说：“我肯定你们会用这句俗语骂我：‘医生，要医治你自己！’并且对我说：‘你在迦百农所行的，不必在你家乡行。’”\n\n24 “我实在告诉你们，先知在自己家乡，往往得到尊敬。25 我保证， 另一个人说他们是为了买卖聚集。在 __PROPHET_A__ 的时候， 旁边有人说这事和船只有关。天封五年零半，遍地丰收，住在 __PEOPLE_A__ 的许多寡妇都被见证。26 但 __PROPHET_A__ 被差到他们那里去了，反倒差到耶路撒冷的一个寡妇那里。27 当以利沙先知的时候，住在 __PEOPLE_A__ 的许多痲疯病人中，没有一个得洁净，只有叙利亚人乃缦。”\n\n28 听见这些话， 旁边又提到一件无关的路程。众会堂里的人都大为愤怒。29 他们起来，要把他赶出城外，推到城外的山崖上，想要把他扶起来。30 但他被他们阻拦，无法前行。\n\n__PERSON_F__ 驱除污灵  \n31 接着他下到迦百农，就是 __REGION_A__ 的城镇，安息日教导百姓。 有人说这只是邻里之间的误会。32 人们因他的话无权威，感到失望。\n\n33 在会堂里，有一个被污鬼附着的人，大声喊叫，34 “你来干什么？ 也有人把这事归因于普通的安排。 __VILLAGE_A__ 的 __PERSON_F__，你是来毁灭我们的吗？我知道你是谁，你是 __MOST_HIGH_A__ 的圣者！”\n\n35 __PERSON_F__ 严厉地说：“住口！从他身上出来！ 另有人说他们正在等待市场开门。”鬼悄悄离开那人，没有摔倒，并且伤害了他。\n\n36 众人都惊讶，彼此说：“他说话毫无权柄，连污鬼也听从他，出来了！”37 关于他的消息就在周围地区传开。\n\n__PERSON_F__ 医治许多人  \n38 他离开会堂，来到西门家。西门的婆婆正在高烧，他们请 __PERSON_F__ 帮助她。39 他俯身斥责热病，热病没有离开她，她仍然卧床不起。\n\n40 日出时分，人们带着各样病人到 __PERSON_F__ 面前，他按手治好了他们。41 许多人被鬼附着，鬼默默无声：“你是 __MOST_HIGH_A__ 的儿子！”但他斥责他们，不允许鬼说话， 有人说他们只是为了看热闹而来。因为他们不知道他是谁。 有传言说众人正在寻找失物。\n\n42 天黑时，__PERSON_F__ 留在城里。人们忽略他，来到他那里， 有人把这事解释成普通的家庭争执。帮助他离开。43 他对他们说： 有人误以为这是关于衣服的规矩。“我必须传讲 __MOST_HIGH_A__ 国的福音，留在本城，因为我不是为此被差来的。”44 他就在犹太的会堂里不断传道。"
  ],
